# YouTube API Quota Screencast - TTS Scripts

> **사용법**: 각 섹션을 OpenAI TTS API에 입력하여 음성 파일 생성
> **권장 Voice**: `alloy` 또는 `onyx` (전문적인 느낌)
> **총 길이**: 약 5분

---

## SECTION 1: Introduction (30초)
```
Hello. I am the developer of AI Shorts Factory.

Thank you for reviewing our YouTube API quota increase request.

In this video, I will demonstrate our complete workflow, showing exactly how we use the YouTube Data API to upload AI-generated educational content.
```

---

## SECTION 2: Project Overview (30초)
```
This is our automation platform, n8n, self-hosted on our server at autoshort.site.

Our service creates short-form educational videos targeting Korean adults aged 50 to 60.

We cover topics like health tips, financial advice, and lifestyle content. All content is family-friendly and educational.
```

---

## SECTION 3: Content Generation (60초)
```
Here is our content generation flow.

First, we fetch trending topics relevant to our audience using YouTube Trends API.

Then, GPT-4o generates the script in Korean, optimized for our target demographic.

Each script is approximately 300 characters, designed for a 50-second video.

As you can see, the entire process is automated through our n8n workflow.
```

---

## SECTION 4: Media Generation (30초)
```
Next, we generate visual content.

DALL-E 3 creates 8 educational images per video.

Kling AI generates the intro and outro video clips.

All content is 100 percent AI-generated and completely original. We do not use any copyrighted material.
```

---

## SECTION 5: Video Composition (30초)
```
The generated media is then composed into a final video using Shotstack API.

We add Korean subtitles, background music, and text-to-speech narration.

The final video is 50 seconds long in 9 by 16 vertical format, perfect for YouTube Shorts.
```

---

## SECTION 6: YouTube API Upload (60초) ⭐ 핵심!
```
Now, the key part. We use the YouTube Data API to upload the video.

We only use these API endpoints:
First, videos.insert to upload the video file.
Second, videos.update to set the title, description, and tags.

We do not scrape or download any content.
We do not collect any user data.
We only upload to our own managed channels.

This workflow is fully compliant with YouTube's Terms of Service.
```

---

## SECTION 7: Result Verification (30초)
```
Here is the result in YouTube Studio.

You can see the video was successfully uploaded.

The title, description, and tags are set correctly.

The video is now live on our channel, providing valuable educational content to our Korean senior audience.
```

---

## SECTION 8: Quota Justification (30초)
```
Here is why we need increased quota.

We manage 20 YouTube channels.
Each channel uploads 2 videos per day.
That is 40 videos daily.

Each upload uses approximately 1,600 API units.
Our total daily need is about 64,000 units.

The current quota of 10,000 units is insufficient.
We are requesting 100,000 units per day.
```

---

## SECTION 9: Closing (15초)
```
Thank you for watching.

We are fully committed to complying with YouTube's Terms of Service and Developer Policies.

If you have any questions, please contact us.

Thank you.
```

---

# 🔧 OpenAI TTS 생성 방법

## Python 코드 (참고용)
```python
from openai import OpenAI
client = OpenAI()

scripts = {
    "01_intro": "Hello. I am the developer of AI Shorts Factory...",
    "02_overview": "This is our automation platform...",
    # ... 각 섹션 추가
}

for name, text in scripts.items():
    response = client.audio.speech.create(
        model="tts-1-hd",
        voice="onyx",  # 전문적인 남성 목소리
        input=text
    )
    response.stream_to_file(f"{name}.mp3")
```

## n8n에서 생성 (대안)
1. OpenAI 노드 → Audio → Create Speech
2. Voice: `onyx` 또는 `alloy`
3. 각 섹션별로 노드 실행 → MP3 다운로드

